{
  "id": "ep187",
  "duration": 50.046,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.478,
      "text": "Billions of planets drift through total darkness without any star at all.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Alone in Space - Astronomers Find New Kind of Planet.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alone_in_Space_-_Astronomers_Find_New_Kind_of_Planet.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.567,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 1.567,
          "end": 4.467,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.478,
      "end": 11.248,
      "text": "Most people assume every single planet belongs to a solar system bound tightly to a shining sun.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Sun With Planets.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sun_With_Planets.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.467,
          "end": 11.233,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.248,
      "end": 18.693,
      "text": "Instead, massive nomadic objects known as rogue planets wander the vast galaxy in absolute solitude.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Icy Earth-mass Rogue Planet (SVS14380).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio - Chris Meaney, Scott Wiessinger, Ashley Balzer",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Icy_Earth-mass_Rogue_Planet_(SVS14380).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.233,
          "end": 18.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.693,
      "end": 28.113,
      "text": "Astronomers first identified a massive population of these mysterious objects back in 2011 using gravitational microlensing techniques.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA21077 Brown Dwarf Microlensing Diagram.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA21077_Brown_Dwarf_Microlensing_Diagram.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.7,
          "end": 24.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 24.133,
          "end": 28.1,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.113,
      "end": 36.183,
      "text": "That clever observational technique reveals invisible worlds when their gravity warps the light of distant background stars.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Gravitational Lensing Diagram (2018-23-4149-Image).png",
        "credit": "IMAGE: NASA, ESA, Ann Feild (STScI), Frank Summers (STScI)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gravitational_Lensing_Diagram_(2018-23-4149-Image).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.1,
          "end": 32.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 32.7,
          "end": 36.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.183,
      "end": 43.833,
      "text": "Recent research suggests these lonely wanderers significantly outnumber star-bound worlds by six to one.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Brown dwarf (artist\u2019s concept) (heic2405a).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, J. Olmsted (STScI)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brown_dwarf_(artist%E2%80%99s_concept)_(heic2405a).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.2,
          "end": 40.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 40.0,
          "end": 43.833,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 43.833,
      "end": 49.696,
      "text": "Trillions of invisible worlds continue drifting through total darkness without any star at all.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Alone in Space - Astronomers Find New Kind of Planet.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alone_in_Space_-_Astronomers_Find_New_Kind_of_Planet.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 43.833,
          "end": 50.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
